{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791752821,"nonce":"A4PDEBwYmlkdcdqd1Mf75eiFuIU=","message":"Decision: the config check piggybacks on GET /activity (edb9ba6) with a 2 s throttle, stat fingerprint then load_settings and a diff against the running settings, not bytes; .env compared by key with in-memory salted digests. Reason: no new timer, bind mounts defeat inotify, comment-only edits show nothing. Decision: RELOADABLE allowlist of fields with a classify-every-field test; paths, console.*, fetch.global_concurrency, api_key_env, catalog_cache and every env or secret change need a restart; the dashboard weekly-cap closures (app.py:351, 397) move to app.state.settings. Reason: those are captured at start in create_app, the fetch semaphore and secrets.startup. Decision: values shown only for an allowlist (caps, scorer specs, ports, models...); contact, alerts address, sender lists, disabled_hosts, provider/referer/title and paths show only changed; errors use loc and msg only, never pydantic input_value. Decision: restart is re-exec with the pre-.env environment on the host, and in containers an exit code 3 with SuccessExitStatus=3 and RestartForceExitStatus=3 opted in via JOBHUNTER_RESTART_EXIT (base unit plus preflight drop-in, open question 2), else the systemctl command. Reason: Restart=on-failure would not restart a clean exit and OnFailure would notify on a non-zero one; a rename-save in a container is only picked up by a new mount (detected via st_nlink 0). Decision: Apply/Restart need a loopback peer, allowed under --allow-remote from a loopback peer. Reason: they spend nothing and act only on the user's file. Decision: restart refused while a console re-score or a claude child runs or the file is invalid; Apply allowed during a re-score. Tickets S12a, S12b.","files":null}]}